kernel sandbox (preview): auto (default); applies: off; would apply: warn
  why: auto applies nothing yet (the kernel sandbox is an opt-in preview)
  permission set: fixed (no prompt can widen it)
  machine: [WILDLINE]enforcer built: no
  policy [WILDLINE] (mode A, self-confined)
    read:       [WILDLINE] + implicit set ([WILDLINE])
    deny read:  none
    write:      [WILDLINE]
    deny write: none
    exec:       no programs
    load code:  [WILDLINE]
    net:        denied
    unix:       denied
    sys:        narrows [WILDLINE]
    env:        not scrubbed
    implicit:   [WILDLINE]
  gaps: [WILDLINE] ([WILDLINE] refused by enforce, marked !)
[WILDCARD]
  ! enforcer [fail-open] --kernel-sandbox: no kernel enforcer for [WILDLINE] is built into this runtime yet: every rule is held by Deno's checks only
